      "slug": "magic-ring-g118",
      "term": "Magic ring",
      "definition": "A starting ring formed by looping the yarn over the fingers and crocheting into the loop before pulling the tail to close the centre hole. Used to begin flat circular pieces without a visible hole at the centre."
    },
    {
      "slug": "crown-increase-g118",
      "term": "Crown increase",
      "definition": "A set of evenly spaced increases worked in the early rounds of a top-down hat. Six increases are placed one per equal section in each round, expanding the circle until the diameter matches the intended head circumference."
    }
  ],
